{
  "$comment": "FROZEN GOLDEN — the builder-vocabulary slice of the catalog the preview server packages, copied byte-for-byte rather than retyped. Issue #819 asks for exactly this: \"Read off the frozen goldens, which ARE the synthesised catalogs, rather than retyped from the source — the source builds these lists partly from constants, and a hand-reconstruction of the Wear set missed remote-compose/custom and remote-compose/inline.\" Nothing in this repository edits this file: it is refreshed by re-copying the slice from the source below, and scripts/foundation-catalog.mjs regenerates compose-foundation.json from it, so a refresh shows up as a reviewable diff in the generated catalog rather than as a silent change of what is served.",
  "schema": "compose-foundation-golden/v1",
  "provenance": {
    "repository": "yschimke/compose-preview-server",
    "path": "docs/design/fixtures/ui-builder/m3-catalog-capabilities-v1.json",
    "commit": "fd8c066b15920d40af07170b9edb6d869764fb22",
    "copiedOn": "2026-09-15",
    "$comment": "The packaged catalog is the donor the synthesised catalogs read from today (ProductionUiBuilderRuntime.baseCatalog -> composeFoundationCatalog), so its builder-namespace components ARE what every published catalog is handed on every request. Its own schema id is compose-ui-builder-capabilities/v1-candidate and the declarations below are unchanged from it.",
    "sourceSchema": "compose-ui-builder-capabilities/v1-candidate"
  },
  "componentMenu": {
    "$comment": "The shelf each builder-namespace id sits on in the PACKAGED (mobile) menu, and the packaged groupOrder it sits in. Carried because a donated component with no shelf sorts after every named one — the failure ui-builder.policy.json's own `menu` comment records for this repository's catalog.",
    "groupOrder": [
      "Scaffolds",
      "Layout",
      "Navigation",
      "Actions",
      "Selection",
      "Text inputs",
      "Containment",
      "Communication",
      "Content",
      "Styles",
